---
layout: default
page_class: "course webinar"
title: "Your AI Provider Will Fail. Design for It."
description: Watch the replay and download the slides from Lee Atchison's webinar on architecting systems that depend on AI components.
---

<%# Replay and slides page for the Sept 30, 2026 webinar. The live deck is
    deliberately not published. The slug mirrors the Kit registration slug
    (softwarearchitectureinsights.com/architecting-with-ai) so the follow-up
    email and the evergreen sequence can point here. The PDF is a copy of the
    file in the webinar's Dropbox "Production Artifacts" folder; replace it
    there first, then here.

    The hero and body reuse the course page's .course-header / .course-body
    styles so the page matches the rest of the site. The "course" page class is
    what makes <main> full-width (see the Webinar pages block in index.css). %>

<% slides_url = relative_url '/downloads/your-ai-provider-will-fail-slides.pdf' %>
<% replay_url = "https://www.linkedin.com/events/7498845868494766080/" %>

<section class="course-header">
  <div class="course-header-inner">
    <div class="course-badge-row">
      <span class="course-platform-badge">Free Webinar</span>
      <span class="course-stat-line">Replay &bull; Slides</span>
    </div>
    <h1><%= data.title %></h1>
    <p class="webinar-lead">Six questions to ask about any AI dependency before it ships.</p>
    <div class="webinar-actions">
      <%# The replay is on LinkedIn, a third-party destination, so it opens in a new tab. %>
      <a href="<%= replay_url %>" class="btn btn-primary" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Watch the Replay &rarr;</a>
      <a href="<%= slides_url %>" class="btn btn-outline" download>Download the Slides</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="course-body">
  <div class="course-body-inner">
    <p>Thanks for your interest in the webinar. The replay and the slides are both free.</p>

    <p>We covered six questions to ask about any AI dependency before it ships, and went deep on the two your existing toolkit gives you nothing for: how would you know an answer was wrong, and what can the model actually reach.</p>

    <%# Title slide, rendered from page 1 of the deck (source render in
        assets_inbox/). Clicking it downloads the deck. %>
    <figure class="webinar-title-slide">
      <a href="<%= slides_url %>" download>
        <img src="<%= relative_url '/images/webinar-architecting-with-ai-title.jpg' %>" width="1280" height="721"
             alt="Title slide: Your AI Provider Will Fail. Design for It.">
      </a>
    </figure>

    <h2>Short clips</h2>

    <p>Three short highlights from the session, on YouTube.</p>

    <%# YouTube Shorts cut from the webinar, also used for marketing.
        Third-party destination, so each opens in a new tab. %>
    <% clips = [
         { label: "The six questions every AI dependency must answer", url: "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/SRvfyylYqJ0" },
         { label: "How to get time and funding for AI reliability", url: "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/Tr6GrevhFdA" },
         { label: "Who owns AI “wrongness” and on-call authority", url: "https://www.youtube.com/shorts/EvdGgv8CNLE" },
       ] %>
    <ul class="webinar-clips">
      <% clips.each do |clip| %>
        <li>
          <a href="<%= clip[:url] %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <span class="webinar-clip-play" aria-hidden="true">&#9654;</span>
            <span class="webinar-clip-label"><%= clip[:label] %></span>
            <span class="webinar-clip-meta">YouTube Short</span>
          </a>
        </li>
      <% end %>
    </ul>

    <h2>Resources</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>
        <a href="<%= replay_url %>" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Webinar replay</strong></a>
        &mdash; watch the full session on LinkedIn.
      </li>
      <li>
        <a href="<%= slides_url %>" download><strong>Webinar slides</strong></a>
        (PDF, 31 pages, 1.9 MB) &mdash; the full deck from the talk.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <%# One sentence of course interest, no link and no ask: the webinar's C20 rule,
        which keeps inbound course interest unprompted until the gate reads. %>
    <p>I'm building a full course on this.</p>
  </div>
</section>
